# Who REVIEWS what — not who writes it.
#
# Each of you writes one side of the app and reviews the other's, so the Mac
# side's paths name LowTechPotato and the Windows side's name mishahatescode.
# GitHub never counts an author's approval of their own pull request: owning
# the paths you usually edit would make every one of your own PRs unmergeable.
#
# With "require review from Code Owners" on, a PR that edits the OTHER side's
# paths needs an approval only its author could give, so it will not merge
# without an admin bypass (mishahatescode only). That is the split doing its
# job: to change the other side, ask the other person.
#
# The last matching line wins.

# Anything not matched below — pubspec, CI, docs, android/ — either can approve.
*                       @mishahatescode @LowTechPotato

# ── Written on the Mac, reviewed from Windows ────────────────────────────────
/lib/ui/                @LowTechPotato
/lib/main.dart          @LowTechPotato
/assets/                @LowTechPotato
/ios/                   @LowTechPotato

# ── Written on Windows, reviewed on the Mac ──────────────────────────────────
/lib/core/              @mishahatescode
/test/                  @mishahatescode

# Widget tests go with whichever side's change they cover — a Mac-side UI fix
# starts with a failing widget test, per CLAUDE.md — so either can approve.
/test/ui/               @mishahatescode @LowTechPotato
